---
// Lead magnet — gates the free AI Native Business book behind a double-opt-in
// email capture. NO Stripe, NO checkout: a pure waitlist-signup opt-in with
// offer=become-ai-native-business; the book is delivered by confirm-email on
// confirm (see supabase/functions/confirm-email). Logo-only header + no footer
// = a 1:1 attention ratio (one action: enter email). The web book stays open
// and indexed; only the download is gated.
//
// 2026-08-15 (operator): the page now ties the free book to Flow, the flagship.
// The book GUIDES (how an AI-native business is structured); Flow TOOLS the
// knowledge worker who has to do that work in a document. Still ONE capture and
// ONE offer key — offer=become-ai-native-business is what confirm-email matches
// to deliver the book, so it must not change. The capture uses the same panel
// treatment as the Flow waitlist so both funnels read as one system. Flow copy
// here stays broad positioning plus the current Mac / subscription facts, no
// mechanism claims.
//
// 2026-08-22: the Flow-state copy on this page branches on ORIONFOLD_FLOW_LIVE
// so one line reverts it with the rest of the site. The FAQ answers are inside
// FAQPage JSON-LD, so a stale one is quoted by answer engines -- they branch too.
// `consentText` does NOT branch, deliberately: it is recorded verbatim into the
// DB on every submit, so a flag flip would fork the compliance record between
// subscribers. It also stays true either way -- this capture still sends Flow
// updates and the digest.
//
// R7e (G-146): a Paper page that keeps the 1:1 attention ratio: a logo that
// is not a link, no nav and a minimal footer. Both captures keep their ids,
// sources, offer key and consent text, inside the Living form bridge.
import PaperLayout from '../layouts/PaperLayout.astro';
import Panel from '../components/paper/Panel.astro';
import Fold from '../components/paper/Fold.astro';
import '../styles/living-in-paper.css';
import WaitlistForm from '../components/ui/WaitlistForm.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { ogMeta } from '../data/og';
import bookCover from '../assets/book/ai-native-business-book.jpg';
import { ORIONFOLD_FLOW_LIVE } from '../data/launch';

const og = ogMeta('/become-ai-native-business/');

// Consent scope now names Flow updates as well as the digest, because that is
// what this capture actually subscribes you to. Recorded verbatim on every
// submit (consent_text), so the stored record matches what the reader agreed to.
const consentText =
  'By subscribing you agree to receive the free book, Orionfold Flow development and launch updates, plus the AI For Everyone digest, one email a week, no more. You can unsubscribe any time. See our privacy policy.';
const privacyNote = consentText.replace(' See our privacy policy.', '');

// What's in the book — marketing-finalized outcome bullets (relay 2026-06-28 §5.2).
const insideBullets = [
  'How an AI-native company is actually structured. The shift from a hierarchy of people to an organization that runs on intelligence.',
  'Where AI does the work, not just the talking. How to refine your data, build your own tools, reuse what works, and put models to the test.',
  'How the pieces hold together at scale. Institutional memory so nothing is relearned, agents that coordinate, and a governance layer you can trust.',
  'Where this is all heading. World models, systems that build their own systems, and what an AI-native business looks like a few years out.',
];

// Objection-as-header blocks (relay 2026-06-28 §5.3). These double as the
// FAQPage schema below, so they are real AEO/citation surface as well as
// conversion copy. Grade 3-5, no em-dashes.
const objections = [
  {
    q: 'Is it really free?',
    a: 'Yes. The full book sells for $20, and you get the same PDF and EPUB at no cost. We ask for your email so we can send the files and one short note a week. That is the whole deal.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What do you do with my email?',
    a: `We send your book, then the AI Native Newsletter (formerly AI For Everyone), one email a week, no more. You also get Orionfold Flow updates${ORIONFOLD_FLOW_LIVE ? ', our Mac app' : ' and the launch note when our Mac app is ready'}. We never sell or rent your address. You can leave any time with one click.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What is Orionfold Flow?',
    a: ORIONFOLD_FLOW_LIVE
      ? 'Flow is our Mac app for the person doing the work. It brings AI to your documents, and you stay the one who approves what changes. The book shows you how an AI-native business is shaped. Flow is the tool for the writing, research, and reporting that shape asks of you. Reading, writing, searching and saving Markdown stay free. AI work needs Flow Pro; Flow Import and Flow Publish are separate paid add-ons to Pro.'
      : 'Flow is the Mac app we are building for the person doing the work. It brings AI to your documents, and you stay the one who approves what changes. The book shows you how an AI-native business is shaped. Flow is the tool for the writing, research, and reporting that shape asks of you. It is in development as a freemium subscription, so there is nothing to buy today.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is this a sales pitch in disguise?',
    a: 'No. The book stands on its own and you can read the whole thing free online too. If you later want our tools, they are there. But the book owes you nothing in return.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who is it for?',
    a: 'Founders and operators who want their business to run on AI, not just chat with it. It is not a guide to building models. It is a guide to running a company that already thinks in AI.',
  },
];

const title = 'Get the free AI Native Business book · Orionfold';
const description =
  'Get the $20 AI Native Business book free. Enter your email for the PDF and EPUB, plus updates on Orionfold Flow, the Mac app for the knowledge worker doing the work.';

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: objections.map((o) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: o.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: o.a },
  })),
};
---
<PaperLayout title={title} description={description} ogImage={og.image} ogImageAlt={og.alt} jsonLd={faqSchema}>
  <header class="pp-done-brand">
    <!-- Logo + wordmark, top-left, subtle and NON-LINKED (marketing 2026-06-28):
         brand presence for trust, but no escape hatch off the page so the only
         action is the email form (max 1:1 attention ratio). -->
    <span class="pp-logo" aria-label="Orionfold"><img src="/logos/orionfold-mark-3d-48.png" alt="" width="24" height="24" />ORIONFOLD</span>
  </header>

  <main id="main" class="pp-page pp-magnet">
    <section class="pp-hero pp-hero--relay pp-magnet-hero" aria-labelledby="magnet-title">
      <!-- Left: the offer + capture -->
      <div class="pp-hero-copy">
        <p class="pp-kicker">Free book · normally $20</p>
        <h1 id="magnet-title" class="pp-h1">Become an AI-native business.</h1>
        <p class="pp-sub">
          Not how to build AI models. How to run a business that already thinks
          in AI.
        </p>
        <p class="pp-magnet-copy">
          Get the $20 <i>AI Native Business</i> book free.
          Just your email, and we send the PDF and EPUB to read on any device.
          You will also get updates on <b>Orionfold Flow</b>,
          {ORIONFOLD_FLOW_LIVE ? 'our Mac app for the person doing the work.' : 'the Mac app we are building for the person doing the work.'}
        </p>

        <!-- Capture panel: the live double-opt-in form inside the Paper form
             sheet. Offer key is unchanged. -->
        <div class="pp-magnet-capture">
          <p class="pp-magnet-chrome"><span>Email only</span><span>Double opt-in</span></p>
          <div class="ls-in-paper ls-form-in-paper">
            <WaitlistForm
              id="magnet-ainb"
              source="magnet-ai-native-business"
              offer="become-ai-native-business"
              buttonText="Send me the book"
              successMessage="Check your inbox to confirm, then your book is on the way."
              consentText={consentText}
            />
          </div>
          <small>
            {privacyNote}{' '}
            <a href="/privacy/">See our privacy policy.</a>
          </small>
        </div>

        <p class="pp-proof">
          Built by one team running private AI on hardware they own: 15 tools, 7
          models, 3 books, and the open-source Orionfold Proof engine.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Right: the cover -->
      <div class="pp-hero-stage">
        <Image
          src={bookCover}
          alt="AI Native Business book cover"
          width={420}
          height={560}
          class="pp-magnet-cover"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <Panel id="inside" seam="What's in the book" fold="atlas">
      <ol class="pp-magnet-inside">
        {insideBullets.map((b) => <li>{b}</li>)}
      </ol>
      <p class="pp-panel-note">Written to be read in about two hours, then kept as a working reference.</p>
    </Panel>

    <!-- Book to Flow tie (operator 2026-08-15). The book is the map; Flow is the
         tool. Copy stays broad positioning plus the current in-development /
         Mac / freemium-planned facts. No mechanism, verification, privacy, or
         pricing claims. -->
    <Panel id="book-and-tool" seam="The book and the tool" tinted>
      <div class="pp-panel-head">
        <h2 id="flow-tie-heading">The book shows you the shape. Flow does the work with you.</h2>
        <p>
          Reading how an AI-native business is put together is the first half. The
          second half is Monday morning, when the writing, the research, and the
          reporting still land on your desk.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="pp-relay-split">
        <div>
          <p class="pp-kicker">The book guides</p>
          <p>
            <i>AI Native Business</i> is the map. How the work is
            structured, where AI does the doing instead of the talking, and how the
            pieces hold together as you grow. Read it in about two hours, then keep
            it as a working reference.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="pp-relay-paid">
          <p class="pp-kicker">Flow tools the work</p>
          <p>
            Orionfold Flow is our Mac app for the knowledge worker. It brings AI
            to your documents, and you stay the one who approves what changes.
            {ORIONFOLD_FLOW_LIVE
              ? ' Markdown stays free. AI work needs Pro; Import and Publish are add-ons.'
              : ' It is in development as a freemium subscription, and your email puts you first in line.'}
          </p>
          <a href="/flow/" class="pp-link">Explore Orionfold Flow <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Panel>

    <!-- Objection blocks (relay §5.3). Header-as-question doubles as FAQPage
         schema (jsonLd above), so every answer stays on the page. -->
    <Panel id="questions" seam="Questions, answered straight">
      <h2 id="faq-heading" class="sr-only">Questions, answered straight</h2>
      <dl class="pp-policy pp-magnet-faq">
        {objections.map((o) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{o.q}</dt>
            <dd>{o.a}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </Panel>

    <!-- Repeated CTA: convertible from any scroll depth (relay §5.5). -->
    <section class="pp-closing" aria-labelledby="cta2-heading">
      <Fold id="atlas" bob class="pp-closing-fold" />
      <h2 id="cta2-heading">Ready when you are.</h2>
      <p>
        Get the $20 <i>AI Native Business</i> book free, and
        {ORIONFOLD_FLOW_LIVE ? 'get the updates on Orionfold Flow.' : 'be first to hear when Orionfold Flow is ready.'}
      </p>
      <div class="pp-magnet-capture">
        <p class="pp-magnet-chrome"><span>Email only</span><span>Double opt-in</span></p>
        <div class="ls-in-paper ls-form-in-paper">
          <WaitlistForm
            id="magnet-ainb-2"
            source="magnet-ai-native-business-footer"
            offer="become-ai-native-business"
            buttonText="Send me the book"
            successMessage="Check your inbox to confirm, then your book is on the way."
            consentText={consentText}
          />
        </div>
        <small>
          {privacyNote}{' '}
          <a href="/privacy/">See our privacy policy.</a>
        </small>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <!-- Minimal footer (relay §5.6): CAN-SPAM needs an unsubscribe path + a
       postal address in the EMAILS only; the page carries the site's
       publisher line (operator 2026-10-30), unsubscribe note, and privacy link. -->
  <footer class="pp-magnet-foot">
    <p>© 2026 Orionfold LLC. Made with ❤️ in Silicon Valley, USA.</p>
    <p>One email a week, no more. Unsubscribe any time from any email we send.</p>
    <p><a href="/privacy/">Privacy policy</a></p>
  </footer>
</PaperLayout>
